      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community was originally called Barrett's Settlement, named after its founder who was known locally as “Uncle Harrison.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/barrett-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1947 a post office and high school opened, after which the area became known as Barrett Station.",
